# Copy this file to .env and change only the lines you actually need.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser. Everything
# below configures the dev server itself and is never sent to the client.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Normal local development (PC browser only) — uncomment these defaults.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_DEV_HOST=127.0.0.1
VITE_DEV_PORT=4173
VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:5000
VITE_DEV_HTTPS=false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LAN mode (opt-in) — comment the block above and uncomment this one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_DEV_HOST=0.0.0.0
# VITE_DEV_PORT=4173
# VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:5000
# VITE_DEV_HTTPS=true
# VITE_HTTPS_CERT_PATH=C:/Users/kalej/oou-k12-certs/oouattendance.home.arpa+1.pem
# VITE_HTTPS_KEY_PATH=C:/Users/kalej/oou-k12-certs/oouattendance.home.arpa+1-key.pem
#
# With VITE_DEV_HOST=0.0.0.0 the dev server listens on every interface, so a
# device on the same local network can load the app. Replace 0.0.0.0 with a
# single address to listen on that interface only.
#
# The address a student opens is this PC's own network address, for example
# http://192.168.0.244:4173. Read it from the machine (ipconfig / ifconfig); it
# is a property of the network, not of this code, and must never be hard-coded in
# application source.
#
# VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET is resolved on this PC, not on the device, so 127.0.0.1
# is correct in LAN mode too. The browser always requests the relative path
# /api/... and the dev server proxies it, so requests stay same-origin: the API
# needs no CORS policy and the HTTP-only session cookies keep working. This is
# why "localhost:5000" never has to appear in frontend code — on a student's
# phone, localhost would mean the phone, not this PC.
#
# VITE_DEV_HTTPS turns on the TLS listener for the LAN HTTPS workflow. The
# certificate and private key must be provided with VITE_HTTPS_CERT_PATH and
# VITE_HTTPS_KEY_PATH. Do not commit these files to Git; keep them outside the
# project or ensure they are ignored by .gitignore.
#
# Setting VITE_DEV_HOST only makes the dev server listen on the local network. It
# does not configure Windows routing, Internet Connection Sharing, NAT, port
# forwarding or firewall rules.
